# MemCan Environment Configuration
#
# Legend:  [REQUIRED] — must be set for secure operation
#          [optional] — has a sensible default, uncomment to override

# --- MemCan Server ---

# [REQUIRED] Bearer token auth for MCP API. Without this, the API is unauthenticated.
MEMCAN_API_KEY=your-secret-key

# [optional] Server bind address (default: 127.0.0.1:8191, Docker overrides to 0.0.0.0:8191)
# MEMCAN_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8191

# [optional] Server URL for thin clients (memcan CLI)
# MEMCAN_URL=http://localhost:8190

# [optional] Log file path. Omit to use the default file; set empty ("") to log to stdout/stderr.
# MEMCAN_LOG_FILE=""

# [optional] Seconds to wait for the next chunk of an incoming /mcp request body before
# failing it with 408. Resets on every chunk, so large uploads are safe. 0 disables it.
# MEMCAN_BODY_READ_TIMEOUT=30

# --- Ollama ---
# Only needed when DISTILL_MEMORIES=true (default). Skip this section if running without LLM.

# [optional] Ollama server URL for LLM inference
# Default: http://ollama:11434 (bundled container) or http://localhost:11434 (standalone)
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# [optional] Bearer token for Ollama endpoint auth (e.g. behind a reverse proxy)
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=your-token-here

# --- LLM Backend Selection ---

# [optional] Two LLM slots, each with its own backend, model, key and endpoint.
# Backends (case-insensitive):
#   ollama                                   local Ollama (defaults: OLLAMA_HOST, OLLAMA_API_KEY)
#   anthropic (alias claude)                 native Anthropic Messages API, prompt caching
#   openai                                   OpenAI API (https://api.openai.com/v1)
#   openrouter                               OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/api/v1)
#   openai-compatible (alias openai-compat)  any OpenAI-compatible API; *_BASE_URL required
# Cloud slots require *_MODEL and *_API_KEY; *_BASE_URL overrides the backend default.
# Any combination works, e.g. two Anthropic keys/models or Anthropic + OpenAI.
# Do not aim openai/openai-compatible/openrouter at api.anthropic.com: its
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint has been observed to reject JSON mode with a 400
# (vendor docs say it is ignored). Use anthropic instead.
# A cloud fallback sends memory, code, and standards content to a third-party
# cloud whenever the primary is unavailable; this is a data-egress trade-off.

# Primary slot (LLM_MODEL defaults to the Ollama model below for ollama)
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=lklimek/gemma4-text:26b-a4b-it-qat
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_BASE_URL=

# Fallback slot
# LLM_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# LLM_FALLBACK_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key
# LLM_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=

# Deprecated: OPENROUTER_API_KEY / OPENROUTER_MODEL / OPENROUTER_BASE_URL still
# configure the first openrouter / openai-compatible slot (with a warning); a set
# slot variable always wins. Exception for pre-slot files: on a primary openrouter
# slot with both LLM_MODEL and OPENROUTER_MODEL set and no per-slot setting in use
# (LLM_API_KEY, LLM_BASE_URL, LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL/_API_KEY/_BASE_URL, or a fallback
# other than ollama/openrouter), LLM_MODEL keeps its old meaning - the Ollama
# model - and moves to an Ollama fallback (or is ignored when there is none);
# OPENROUTER_MODEL is the primary model. An openrouter fallback with no settings
# of its own duplicates the primary and is dropped. Startup logs which value
# went where.

# --- Storage ---

# [optional] LanceDB storage path (embedded — no server needed)
# LANCEDB_PATH=~/.local/share/memcan/lancedb

# [optional] Default user ID for memory scoping
# DEFAULT_USER_ID=global

# --- LLM & Embeddings ---

# [optional] Memory distillation (LLM fact extraction + dedup)
# Set to false to run without Ollama — stores memories as-is
# DISTILL_MEMORIES=true

# Ollama model: set it as the Ollama slot's *_MODEL (see LLM slots above). The
# default lklimek/gemma4-text:26b-a4b-it-qat needs ~16GB VRAM (projector-free
# build, full GPU residency on a 16GB card); use qwen3.5:9b on smaller GPUs.

# [optional] Embedding model — fastembed in-process ONNX model name
# EMBED_MODEL=MultilingualE5Large

# --- Traefik / Networking (Docker only) ---

# [optional] IP allowlist for Traefik middlewares (applies to memcan, ollama, webui)
# Default: localhost only (IPv4 + IPv6). Add your network CIDR to allow remote access.
# TRAEFIK_IP_ALLOWLIST=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128

# --- Docker Compose ---

# [optional] Profiles to enable. "ollama" starts the bundled Ollama container.
# "ollama,webui" also starts Open WebUI. Leave empty to use an external Ollama.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=ollama

# [optional] Rust log level for memcan container
# RUST_LOG=info,memcan_core=debug,memcan_server=debug

# [optional] Host path for Ollama model storage (default: Docker named volume)
# OLLAMA_DATA_DIR=ollama-data
